WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.934
-Welcome back. Welcome back.
No, please, after you.

00:00:03.934 --> 00:00:06.701
Oh, after you.
No, after you, of course. Yeah.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:08.834
It is so great to see you, bud.
-Thank you.

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:11.234
Everybody should have that
experience once in their life.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.534
Walk into a room
with The Roots playing.

00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:15.133
-Exactly, yeah.
-There's nothing like that.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.367
-How does it feel to be in front
of an audience and a crowd?

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.634
I mean, they love you.
Come on, bud.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.501
-Hi, everyone.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.467
-Last time we were
with each other together

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.167
was almost 11 years ago.

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:31.300
Does that --
-It feels like 20.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.501
-It feels like yesterday.
But, I mean, a lot has changed.

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:36.300
We're dads now.
-That's right. Congratulations.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.467
-Congratulations to you. Yeah.
-Thank you.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.767
-How does it feel?
-It's the greatest.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:41.801
-Yeah. How old are they?

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:43.133
Are they around
the same as mine?

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:46.133
-6 and 7. Yours are...
-8 and -- Yeah, 7 and 8, yeah.

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:47.367
-Okay.

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.200
-My girls are a little bit
starting to not laugh at

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.267
every joke that I tell.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:51.434
-Oh, okay.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:52.434
-'Cause they used to be
my number-one fan.

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:53.534
I'd do anything,
they'd be like...

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.501
[ Laughs ]
..."Fantastic."

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.834
Now they just sometimes
don't react or

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.334
I get the eye roll or something.

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:01.434
You're like, "Did you just
roll your eyes at me?

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:02.767
I mean, it's cute,
but don't do that."

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:04.200
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.300
-My youngest has a real power
move where she'll, like --

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.601
Here's an example.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:12.334
We got to work in France,
and so we went to The Louvre

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:14.067
and we saw, you know,
"Winged Victory."

00:01:14.067 --> 00:01:15.534
We saw "Venus de Milo."

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.100
And we're standing
in front of the "Mona Lisa,"

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.834
and she turns around
and she goes, "This museum?"

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:28.734
And I said --
-Only kids.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:29.801
-I said, "Why?"
-Yeah.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.434
-And she went,
"Because it is not good."

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:33.501
-Yeah. N.G.
N.G., man.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.234
-And then the real power move
is, sometimes,

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:37.501
she'll turn around
and she'll just go...

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:43.400
The thumbs-down walk-away.
-Walk away.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.334
Oh, that's a fantastic move.

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:48.734
-It's like
Roman-emperor-level shade.

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:51.634
-Just walking away with
the thumbs down is a power move.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:52.767
I want to ask you
about this photo.

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:54.100
-Okay.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:55.434
-I just want to ask you
questions about it.

00:01:55.434 --> 00:01:57.267
I saw --
-Okay.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:01:58.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:03.334
-It broke -- It officially broke
the Internet.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:04.567
-Well, you know, the Internet's

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:05.634
been trying to
break me for years.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:06.634
-Yeah. And they finally got you.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.834
-So they gave me
no other choice.

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.667
You are Ken
in the new "Barbie" movie.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.567
And this is fantastic.

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:15.234
Were you surprised by the
great reaction this photo got?

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:19.467
-I was surprised how, you know,
some people were kind of

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:21.167
clutching their pearls
about my Ken,

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:23.100
as though they ever
thought about Ken

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.467
for a second before this.

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:25.601
-Yeah, you feel like
he's underappreciated.

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:26.934
-They never played with Ken.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.534
-Underappreciated character,
Ken.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:29.667
-They never played with Ken.

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:31.000
Nobody plays with Ken, man.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.968
-You don't really play with Ken.
-Did you play with Ken?

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:34.133
-Um...
-Exactly.

00:02:34.133 --> 00:02:35.767
-No, I didn't play with him.
-Exactly.

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:38.334
-It was available.
-And yet...

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:39.701
-He stayed in the toy box.

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:44.334
-He's an accessory and not even
one of the cool ones.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.100
-He's an accessory of
Barbies, yeah.

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.067
She's got the camper.
-The house.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.367
-The house.

00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.300
It's unbelievable,
what she's done with the house.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.434
Have you ever put together one
of those houses, by the way?

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:58.067
-I tried.
-I want to sue Mattel.

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:00.767
I had -- So mad.
I was like, "Oh, my gosh.

00:03:00.767 --> 00:03:02.767
This is the craziest thing
to put together ever,"

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:03.901
the Dreamhouse.

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:04.968
And that's it.

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.901
We have the house
and now we live in it.

00:03:06.901 --> 00:03:08.501
It took so long.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:09.534
But you know what?

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:12.367
There was a thing in
"Vanity Fair."

00:03:12.367 --> 00:03:15.000
They said they think they know
why you chose the role of Ken --

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.534
because you have
a love of Jean jackets.

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:20.567
-Oh.
-And...

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.300
That's you throughout the years
loving the jean jacket.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.801
I do like a good jean jacket
if I can rock it.

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:29.434
But that is not the reason
why you chose Ken.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:31.801
-Did you bring me on your show
to denim-shame me?

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:33.334
-Yeah.
-Is that what this is?

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.534
There's no denim shame
in my game, man.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:37.300
-No way, man. I love your denim.
-I love denim.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.467
-No, I want to set up this story
because it made me laugh.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:41.634
You're like, "No, the reason why
I took this role --"

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:43.133
You got a call from
Greta Gerwig -- or an e-mail.

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:44.367
-Right.

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:47.901
-From Greta, who's a great
actor, director, writer.

00:03:47.901 --> 00:03:49.501
And she offered you
the role of Ken.

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:50.801
-Yes.

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:52.267
-And you went out in
your backyard and you were --

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.000
You know, you want to
think about it for a second.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.567
You go in the backyard.
-Best script I've ever read.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:57.868
I walk out in the backyard.

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:00.501
And do you know where
I found Ken, Jimmy?

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:03.000
Facedown in the mud
next to a squished lemon.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.701
-And this is the photo --
You took a photo of it.

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:07.267
And this is a sign.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:09.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:13.334
This is a sign
that you got to do this movie.

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:15.234
The utter disrespect.

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:18.534
-I texted it to Greta and
I said, "I shall be your Ken.

00:04:18.534 --> 00:04:21.133
For his story must be told."

00:04:21.133 --> 00:04:22.667
-Yeah, his story must be told.

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:26.601
I want to hear this guy -- What
happened to the situation here?

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:29.200
I know you're doing press for
"The Gray Man,"

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.000
but people were asking
you about the "Barbie" movie,

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.133
and you -- Then they go,
you know, "What is it about?"

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:35.701
And you go,
"Well, Ken has no house,

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:38.067
you know, "No home and no job."

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:40.534
And they're like,
"Is this a drama?

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:42.334
Is this a sad --"
-Those are not plot details.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:45.868
Those are just
objective facts about Ken.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.200
-It has nothing to do
with the movie.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.567
The movie is not about
Ken having no house or a job.

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.834
-No. Those are just --
That's the Ken life.

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.701
-Yeah, that's just the Ken life.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:54.834
-Yeah, I just wanted to
straighten that out

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:56.000
for anyone that's going like,

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.133
"That's not what the
'Barbie' movie is about."

00:04:57.133 --> 00:04:58.667
It's going to be --
What a cast, by the way.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:00.601
I cannot wait.
Everyone you can think of.

00:05:00.601 --> 00:05:02.133
It's going to be
funny and awesome.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:03.133
I want to talk about
"The Gray Man."

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:04.601
-Okay.

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:07.734
-Dude, talk about action on top
of action on top of action.

00:05:07.734 --> 00:05:09.667
-And then more action.
-And then more action.

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.033
-And then some sneaky action.

00:05:11.033 --> 00:05:12.100
-Yeah, and they snuck
a little action in there.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.200
-They snuck
a little action in there.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:14.267
-Yeah.

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:15.767
-Do you know,
in most action films,

00:05:15.767 --> 00:05:19.501
there's like four to five action
moments, big action moments?

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.334
-Yeah.
-This has nine, Jimmy.

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:23.167
-Yeah.
-That's four and five.

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:26.067
-Wow. That's five added
action sequences.

00:05:26.067 --> 00:05:28.167
-We pack the action.
-Yes, you do.

00:05:28.167 --> 00:05:29.834
-It's action-packed.
-It's action-packed.

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:32.267
And you've got my man,
Chris Evans, as well, in this.

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:33.868
And, yeah, look at that.

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:36.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:42.067
Also, I must say, you're rockin'
some pretty awesome facial hair.

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:43.400
You got the goatee.
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.067
-He's got the mustache.
-Yeah.

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:47.334
Our facial hair
had different acting styles.

00:05:47.334 --> 00:05:50.467
His mustache went to
the Stella Adler School,

00:05:50.467 --> 00:05:52.033
and my goatee was Meisner.

00:05:52.033 --> 00:05:53.167
-Meisner, of course.

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:55.400
-And it's electric on set,
but it's --

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.801
Off camera, it is trouble.

00:05:57.801 --> 00:05:59.067
-What is "The Gray Man" about?

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:00.734
What do people --
What should they expect,

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:02.467
besides action and fun?

00:06:02.467 --> 00:06:04.901
-It starts with action.
-Mm-hmm.

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:06.567
-Then you find out this
character --

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.033
They pull him out of prison
to be a spy,

00:06:08.033 --> 00:06:09.033
but he doesn't want to be
a spy, Jimmy.

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:10.467
-Of course not.

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:12.467
-He'd rather be at home watching
Netflix, like the rest of us.

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:14.767
-Yeah, exactly. Of course.
-But he can't.

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:16.868
He has to.
They're forcing him to do it.

00:06:16.868 --> 00:06:18.834
The only way he gets out...
-Is to go back in.

00:06:18.834 --> 00:06:20.734
-...more action.
-Yes! That's exactly right!

00:06:20.734 --> 00:06:22.601
-Amazing cast,
amazing characters,

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:25.033
and then we close it out with
so much action.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:26.501
-There you go.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:28.501
Here's Ryan Gosling in
"The Gray Man."

00:06:28.501 --> 00:06:29.734
Take a look at this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.734 --> 00:06:30.801
-Give me the gun.

00:06:33.634 --> 00:06:35.167
[ Tires squeal ]

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:37.334
♪♪

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:50.567
-Get down!

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:55.701
You're in my shot.

00:06:55.701 --> 00:06:58.300
-You gave me an empty gun?

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.167
-The shells were coming, okay?
-Huh?

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:02.167
-The shells were coming.
You -- You ran away too fast.

00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:04.767
-Then you need to say,
"Hey, wait. That's empty."

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:06.033
-No, it's assumed.

00:07:06.033 --> 00:07:09.000
-I assumed it's loaded,
so I run after the guy.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.367
-Who throws a loaded gun?

00:07:10.367 --> 00:07:11.534
-I asked for a loaded gun.

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:13.234
-No one throws
a loaded weapon, okay?

00:07:13.234 --> 00:07:15.334
Are you coming?

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.200
-Ugh!

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.200
-I'm going to bleed out
while we have this conversation.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.434
Can we just
unpack this somewhere else?

00:07:21.434 --> 00:07:24.467
-Yeah. Let's just unpack this
somewhere else.

00:07:24.467 --> 00:07:26.834
That's what I'm talking about
right there.

00:07:26.834 --> 00:07:29.868
Ryan Gosling, "The Gray Man,"
everybody.

00:07:29.868 --> 00:07:31.934
Thank you for being here.
-Thank you, man.

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:33.634
Should we talk about it now?

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:36.033
-Is it grossing you out?
-Should we talk about this?

00:07:36.033 --> 00:07:37.400
-Wait. Hold on a second.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:38.467
[ Music starts, stops ]

00:07:38.467 --> 00:07:40.000
It's gross.
Is it grossing you out?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.067
-What's going on with
the nail, man?

00:07:41.067 --> 00:07:43.133
-My nail was --
Yeah, I hit my nail.

00:07:43.133 --> 00:07:45.167
-What's happened?
-I have a black nail.

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:46.267
-Yeah.
-You know what happened?

00:07:46.267 --> 00:07:47.834
There's a screen door.

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:50.200
I slammed my pinkie
in a screen door.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.501
I was holding the screen.

00:07:51.501 --> 00:07:52.901
It was one of those screen doors
that go like...

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:54.200
[ Hisses ]

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:55.300
And I go, "Oh, that's nice."

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:56.367
And then, all of a sudden,
it went, "Whap!"

00:07:56.367 --> 00:07:58.667
And so it got me.
Is it bumming you out?

00:07:58.667 --> 00:08:01.200
-It looks fungusy.
-It's black.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.300
It's not fungusy.
It's just black.

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:03.334
[ Audience groans ]

00:08:03.334 --> 00:08:06.267
-You know, I have --
-Sorry. We --

00:08:06.267 --> 00:08:09.067
-Having two little girls,
I have...

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:13.667
Just saying, if you want --
I mean, it is...

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:15.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:18.968
Shall we?
-Will you do the honors?

00:08:18.968 --> 00:08:23.334
-It is -- I mean, Jimmy, you're
in the public eye right now.

00:08:23.334 --> 00:08:24.601
-This is --
-There you go.

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:26.000
-You did a great job.
-Thanks.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.234
-Look at that. Look at this.
It's like nothing ever happened.

00:08:28.234 --> 00:08:30.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:30.133 --> 00:08:32.701
This is fantastic.
You did a great job.

00:08:32.701 --> 00:08:34.167
Ryan Gosling, everybody.

00:08:34.167 --> 00:08:37.734
"The Gray Man" begins
streaming on Netflix tomorrow.

00:08:37.734 --> 00:08:39.734
When we come back, Ryan and I
are doing something fun.

00:08:39.734 --> 00:08:41.133
Stick around.
♪♪

